  "executive_briefing": "In August 2026, the digital asset ecosystem is navigating a pivotal legislative intermission alongside structural shifts in cross-chain capital deployment. The U.S. Senate's decision to postpone the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633) vote until mid-September has intensified negotiations surrounding market structure and smart contract regulation. In institutional markets, Bitcoin ETF products are shifting from an aggressive accumulation phase into structured treasury management and capital efficiency playbooks. Meanwhile, Ethereum maintains its foundation as the primary EVM smart contract benchmark, while non-custodial cross-chain routing protocols (such as Symbiosis, deBridge, and THORChain) are breaking down silos between native Bitcoin liquidity and EVM networks.",
